---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ExamShell from "../../../components/ExamShell.astro";
import ExamPractice from "../../../components/ExamPractice.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="B1 for Italian citizenship: mock test and practice – icanspeak Italian"
  description="The B1 language proof on the path to Italian citizenship: which certificates count, how they are marked and free practice with our own mock and a reading test. General orientation, not legal advice."
>
  <ExamShell
    bild="dtz"
    header="B1 for citizenship"
    title="B1 for Italian citizenship"
    titleKey="dtz.title"
    lead="Most adults who apply for Italian citizenship by residence or marriage must show Italian at B1, usually with a certificate from a recognised exam (CILS, CELI, PLIDA or CERT.IT). Here you can read how that works and practise with our own mock."
    leadKey="dtz.lead"
    badges={["B1"]}
    practiceHeading="Practise for the B1 language proof"
    practiceHeadingKey="dtz.practiceHeading"
  >
    <Fragment slot="info">
      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="dtz.who.title">Who is this for?</h2>
        <div class="exam-meta-row">
          <span class="exam-meta-badge" data-i18n="dtz.who.badge.result">Level B1</span>
          <span class="exam-meta-badge" data-i18n="dtz.who.badge.course">For the citizenship path</span>
        </div>
        <p data-i18n="dtz.who.text">
          For citizenship by residence or marriage, the usual language proof is a certificate at B1 or
          higher from one of the recognised certifying bodies: CILS, CELI, PLIDA or CERT.IT. Some people
          are exempt, for example some holders of Italian school or university qualifications. The rules
          changed in 2025 and can change again, so check the official sources before you book. This is
          general orientation, not legal advice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="exam.skills.title">Skills tested</h2>
        <div class="skill-grid">
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">📖</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.lesen">Lesen</h4><p data-i18n="skill.lesen.desc">Leseverstehen</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">🎧</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.hoeren">Hören</h4><p data-i18n="skill.hoeren.desc">Hörverstehen</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">✍️</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.schreiben">Schreiben</h4><p data-i18n="dtz.skill.schreiben.desc">Written tasks</p></div>
          <div class="skill-card"><div class="skill-card-icon">🗣️</div><h4 data-i18n="skill.sprechen">Sprechen</h4><p data-i18n="skill.sprechen.oralDesc">Spoken expression</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="exam-section">
        <h2 data-i18n="dtz.format.title">How our mock is built</h2>
        <div class="format-table-wrap">
          <table class="format-table">
            <thead><tr><th data-i18n="format.th.part">Part</th><th data-i18n="format.th.what">What it tests</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.listen1.part">Listening: messages and radio</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.listen1.what">Short announcements, phone messages and radio items, with one question each</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.listen2.part">Listening: conversations and opinions</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.listen2.what">Everyday conversations with two tasks each; three people matched to what they think</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read1.part">Reading: contents page and adverts</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read1.what">Find the right chapter in a guide; match situations to adverts</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read2.part">Reading: short texts and rules</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read2.what">An email, a forum, local news and a set of rules or a contract</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read3.part">Reading: an email with gaps</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.read3.what">Choose the word that fits each gap</td></tr>
              <tr><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.write.part">Writing</td><td data-i18n="dtz.fmt.write.what">One message or email from a choice of two, with a model answer and a checklist</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="format-note" data-i18n-html="dtz.format.note">
          This is the structure of our own mock, not of a real exam. For the real parts and timings, see
          the certifying body of your exam and our <a href="/cils/b1">CILS B1 practice set</a>. The mock
          has no speaking part: practise that with our
          <a href="/parlato/serie/a2-out-and-about">speaking tasks</a>. The extra
          <a href="/lettura-e-scrittura">reading &amp; writing</a> tasks are good for more practice.
        </p>

        <h3 data-i18n="dtz.scoring.title">How the B1 certificates are marked</h3>
        <p data-i18n-html="dtz.scoring.text">
          Each certificate has its own marking rule, published by its certifying body, and the result is
          a pass or a fail (<em>superato</em> or <em>non superato</em>). In our mock the point bands are
          <strong>our own guide</strong>, not an official score.
        </p>
      </section>
    </Fragment>

    <div class="mock-cta mock-cta--lead">
      <h2 data-i18n="dtz.set.title">Our B1 mock: listening, reading and writing</h2>
      <p data-i18n="dtz.set.text">
        Our own mock in exam style: listening and reading parts, plus a writing task with a model
        answer. You can run a clock for each skill. At the end you see your result by part, with our own
        point bands as a guide. Progress stays saved in the browser.
      </p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/cittadinanza/prova-b1/esercitazione" data-i18n="exam.startSet">Start the practice set</a>
      <a class="plan-link" href="/piano-d-esame" data-i18n="plan.link">Your plan up to the exam →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mock-cta">
      <h2 data-i18n="dtz.path.title">The whole path to citizenship</h2>
      <p data-i18n="dtz.path.text">Which proofs you need, who is exempt and the order of the steps.</p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/cittadinanza" data-i18n="dtz.path.cta">See the path</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mock-cta">
      <h2 data-i18n="dtz.mock.title">Kürzer: Mock-Test Lesen (Aufgabe 1–4)</h2>
      <p data-i18n="dtz.mock.text">All four reading tasks as one continuous test at level B1, with an overall result at the end.</p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/cittadinanza/prova-b1/simulazione" data-i18n="dtz.mock.start">Mock-Test starten</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mock-cta">
      <h2 data-i18n="fallen.title">Exam traps</h2>
      <p data-i18n="fallen.entry.blurb">Spots with a catch – briefly explained, with an example and a task to try.</p>
      <a class="quiz-btn quiz-btn--primary" href="/esami/trappole" data-i18n="fallen.entry.cta">Fallen ansehen</a>
    </div>

    <ExamPractice
      heading="Grundlagen trainieren"
      headingKey="exam.practice.heading"
      intro="These practice tools train the skills a B1 exam tests."
      introKey="dtz.practice.intro"
      tools={["artikel", "grammatik", "wortschatz", "sprechen", "lesen"]}
    />
  </ExamShell>
</Layout>
